  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), leaving virtually no information about whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal. The majority of the remaining search space (configs 016–051) is multimodal, so the value of that entire branch hinges on whether image features are informative at all. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image modality with a standard, well-understood encoder, giving a clean baseline for image performance without confounding from fusion, aggregation, or multiprofile. Why this is the best use of the next budget: If image_only substantially exceeds or falls below the RNA-only baseline, it immediately reshapes strategy—validating or deprioritizing the entire multimodal branch and guiding whether to invest subsequent experiments in fusion/aggregation or in improving the RNA side. No other single experiment reduces uncertainty across such a large portion of the search space."
}

